/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload

# Viz embed routes are <iframe> targets, so they must be frameable cross-origin.
# They're distinct paths, so scope framing to them: drop the global
# X-Frame-Options DENY and allow any framer via CSP frame-ancestors.
# VERIFY AT CUTOVER on Cloudflare Pages with a real cross-origin iframe on a
# deploy preview — per-path header override/unset semantics differ by host
# (Cloudflare Pages supports `! Header` to unset a value set by a broader rule;
# if that doesn't take effect, restructure so `/*` doesn't set X-Frame-Options
# and instead deny framing per-path, or enforce anti-framing at the edge).
/cohend/embed
  ! X-Frame-Options
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *

# Permanent: legacy embeds frame the main page as /cohend?embed=1, and
# X-Frame-Options would block that document before its client-side redirect
# (to /cohend/embed, in src/routes/cohend/+page.svelte) could run. The page
# has no auth/cookies/actions, so frameability costs ~nothing, and the
# changelog promises old links are never dropped — don't "harden" this back
# to DENY. Exact-path match: /cohend/changelog is not affected.
/cohend
  ! X-Frame-Options
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors *
